  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one data point (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), which serves as a weak baseline. The central question for a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether adding the image modality improves over the RNA-only baseline. This experiment (config_016: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the cleanest direct comparison to config_001—it keeps the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000) and profile setting (singleprofile), changing only the addition of an image branch (resnet50) with the simplest fusion (concat). This isolates the effect of modality addition without confounding from encoder choice, aggregation, or fusion complexity. If multimodal outperforms 48.5%, we gain strong evidence to exploit multimodal variants in remaining experiments; if not, we redirect budget toward improving single-modality representations (better RNA encoders or image encoders). With 8 experiments left, resolving this pivotal question early maximizes the information value of subsequent choices."
}

